  "question": {
    "text": "The number of solution to the equation <math><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi></math> where <math><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>N</mi></math>, is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "36",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math><br />Note that <math><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></math> are divisible by <math><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> hence <math><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math> is divisible by <math><mn>3</mn></math><br />Similarly <math><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>60</mn></math> are even numbers hence <math><mn>3</mn><mi>b</mi></math> is an even number<br />Therefore <math><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msub><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math><br />So the equation reduces to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8704;</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>N</mi></math><br />Hence, the number of solutions <math><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi></mi></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow></mmultiscripts></math>",
    "image": null
  },
